]11;#000000]10;#6a9955]4;0;#000000]4;1;#6a9955]4;2;#6a9955]4;3;#6a9955]4;4;#6a9955]4;5;#6a9955]4;6;#6a9955]4;7;#6a9955]4;8;#3a5945]4;9;#6a9955]4;10;#00ff00]4;11;#6a9955]4;12;#6a9955]4;13;#6a9955]4;14;#6a9955]4;15;#00ff00usage: code-puppy [-h] [--version] [--interactive] [--prompt PROMPT]
                  [--agent AGENT] [--model MODEL] [--resume PATH]
                  [--quick-resume [PATH]] [--no-tools] [--yolo {true,false}]
                  [--acp]
                  [command ...]

Code Puppy - A code generation agent

positional arguments:
  command               Run a single command (deprecated, use -p instead)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version, -v         Show version and exit
  --interactive, -i     Run in interactive mode
  --prompt, -p PROMPT   Execute a single prompt and exit (no interactive mode)
  --agent, -a AGENT     Specify which agent to use (e.g., --agent code-puppy)
  --model, -m MODEL     Specify which model to use (e.g., --model gpt-5)
  --resume, -r PATH     Resume a saved session from a .pkl file (e.g.
                        ~/.code_puppy/contexts/foo.pkl)
  --quick-resume, -qr [PATH]
                        Resume the most recent session for PATH (defaults to
                        the current directory; scopes to git root + branch
                        when available)
  --no-tools            Disable all agent tools and MCP servers for this run
                        (pure text-in/text-out; equivalent to
                        CODE_PUPPY_NO_TOOLS=1)
  --yolo {true,false}   Override YOLO mode for this run without changing
                        puppy.cfg (/set yolo_mode takes precedence)
  --acp                 Run as a native agent over the Agent Client Protocol
                        (ACP), speaking JSON-RPC over stdio.
